Ping the dispatcher destinations that have flag 16 again, as Kamailio 5.8 did.

Kamailio 6.0 and later skip them in ds_ping_set() (kamailio/kamailio#4150,
commit 1515099f5b, "dispatcher: skip ping for DS_NODNSARES_DST"). A
destination whose name may not resolve when the list loads, such as when the
network or DNS isn't up yet, needs flag 16 to stay in the list: without it,
the dispatcher drops the line, and nothing adds it back until a reload.
Without pings, such a destination never becomes inactive while no call goes
to it, and once a call marks it inactive, only the next ping that clears
flag 16 brings it back.

The skip guards against a ping's state update clearing flag 16 of a
destination whose name has no A record by definition, such as one with SRV
or NAPTR records only: after the RPC commands dispatcher.add or
dispatcher.remove, which rebuild a set from memory, the dispatcher looks such
a destination up and drops it. Kamailio 5.8 did the same. Don't use flag 16
for such destinations together with these RPC commands.

Remove this patch when Kamailio pings flag-16 destinations again, or makes
the skip optional. The role fails the build when the patch doesn't apply to
the version that it builds.

--- a/src/modules/dispatcher/dispatch.c
+++ b/src/modules/dispatcher/dispatch.c
@@ -4609,9 +4609,6 @@
 		/* skip addresses with no-ping flag */
 		if((node->dlist[j].flags & DS_NOPING_DST) != 0)
 			continue;
-		/* skip addresses with no-DNS-A flag */
-		if((node->dlist[j].flags & DS_NODNSARES_DST) != 0)
-			continue;
 		/* If the Flag of the entry has "Probing set, send a probe:	*/
 		if(ds_ping_result_helper(node, j)) {
 			LM_DBG("probing set #%d, URI %.*s\n", node->id,
